We defined a relevance function $ \phi(y) $ using the \texttt{extremes} method with three control points:

\begin{align*}
\phi(y) = 
\begin{cases}
1       & \text{if } y = \min(\mathcal{Y}) \\
0.025   & \text{if } y = \mu = \mathrm{mean}(\mathcal{Y}) \\
0       & \text{if } y = \max(\mathcal{Y})
\end{cases}
\end{align*}

where $\mathcal{Y}$ denotes the set of target values in the training data. The relevance function smoothly interpolates between these points to emphasize extreme values.





