\mysection{Prefactor $\chi$  \label{App:chi}}
%%%  chi
The factor $\chi$ is defined by Eq. \eqref{eq:chidef}.
Constructing the ratio of $\Gamma$ functions (App. C of \cite{DW25}), one obtains
\beeq\label{eq:Achi}
\chi(k,\gamma) &\approx & \frac{e}{\sqrt{2\pi}}\, \sqrt{\frac{1+k}{(1+\gamma k)(1+(1-\gamma)k)}} \cdot \frac{\cR(k)}{\cR(\gamma k) \cR((1-\gamma)k) } , \\
\cR(k) &=& \big(1+ k^{-1}\big)^k \left(1+ \frac1{12(1+k)^2} \right)^{(1+k)} .
\eeeq
There is a mismatch between \eqref{eq:Achi} and the expression that was announced as the answer for $\chi(k,\gamma)$ in Eq. (C.7) of \cite{DW25}, due to the unnecessary simplifications made there. 

We stress that the full expression \eqref{eq:Achi} was used for the calculations throughout both papers.

The function $\chi$ depends on the scale via the anomalous dimension $\gamma(\as(Q))$ both explicitly and implicitly through the characteristic moment rank $\chi =\chi(\ksd(\nu, \gamma), \gamma) $.
