For any subgroup $H\le G$, we denote $\overline{H}$ as the closure of $\iota_G(H)$ in $\widehat{G}$. Note that $H$ does not always inject into $\overline{H}$, for instance, when $G$ is not residually finite. In addition, the surjective homomorphism $\widehat{H}\to \overline{H}$ is an isomorphism if and only if the condition in \autoref{PROP: Left exact} holds.

