\begin{proposition}[{\cite[Proposition 6.15]{Wil19}}]\label{PROP: FPinfty pair}
Suppose $(X,Y)$ is an Eilenberg-MacLane pair for a discrete group pair $(G,\mathcal{H})$, and $X$ has finitely many cells in each dimension. Then $(G,\mathcal{H})$ is of type $\text{FP}_\infty$. 
