 \centering
 \includegraphics[width=3.3in]{overview.png}
 \caption{Hi-D Maps: multiple dimensions mapped to a regular polygon. The polygon is cut hierarchically with lines parallel to the sides corresponding to the dimensions. The area of a leaf polygon is proportional to the size of the corresponding data intersection. The full dataset is displayed in the left overview window; as the mouse hovers over a subset, it is magnified in the right detail window.}
 \label{overview}
