To investigate runtime stability further, we performed three evaluation runs with 10,000 trajectories each on the ARM System. Figure~\ref{fig:runtime_boxplot} shows the resulting boxplots. Across all runs, the latencies remain tightly clustered, with only a few outliers. These deviations appear randomly and do not correlate with specific trajectory indices, suggesting that the underlying cause is unrelated to input structure and more likely rooted in occasional system-level effects such as memory contention or interrupt handling.

